---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Code.astro";
import Note from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Note.astro";
import { u } from "../../data/nav";
import { version } from "../../data/version";
---
<Docs title="Installation" lede="Add the kit from npm, from pip for Python, or link the hosted files.">
  <h2>JavaScript projects</h2>
  <p>The whole kit is one package on npm.</p>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`npm install @dario-loi/polytope`} />
  <p>To install straight from GitHub instead, npm 12 needs the project to allow git dependencies, and the address needs quotes for zsh. Upgrading a git install means uninstalling first, so the registry is the easier path.</p>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`echo "allow-git=root" >> .npmrc
npm install "github:dario-loi/polytope#v${version}"`} />
  <p>What the package exports:</p>
  <div class="ply-table-wrap">
    <table class="ply-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Import path</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/css</code></td><td>Everything: fonts, tokens, every component. One file.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/tokens.css</code></td><td>Only the custom properties, for projects that bring their own components.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/css/button.css</code></td><td>One component at a time. Needs <code>tokens.css</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/js/all.js</code></td><td>The scripts: probability machine, copy buttons, theme toggle, on-this-page list.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/astro</code></td><td>Astro components.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/tokens</code></td><td>Tokens as a JavaScript module, with TypeScript types.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@dario-loi/polytope/tokens.json</code></td><td>Tokens as flat JSON, with light and dark values.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The <a href={u("/getting-started/targets/")}>other targets</a> page lists the Tailwind, Sass, LaTeX, Figma, and editor exports.</p>

  <h2>Using Polytope with Impeccable</h2>
  <p><a href="https://impeccable.style/">Impeccable</a> is a design skill for AI coding agents such as Claude Code. It reads a project's visual system from <code>DESIGN.md</code> and <code>.impeccable/design.json</code> in its root. The package ships both, and one command copies them into a site:</p>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`npx @dario-loi/polytope            # copies DESIGN.md and .impeccable/design.json
npx @dario-loi/polytope --check    # fails if the copies are older than the installed Polytope`} />
  <p>In a project that has Polytope installed, npx runs that copy. The command will not replace another system's <code>DESIGN.md</code> unless you pass <code>--force</code>. Copy the files again after upgrading Polytope, and add the check to the site's CI to catch a stale copy.</p>
  <p>A site without npm, such as a static site built by a Python script, can fetch the same two files pinned to a release, and link the hosted stylesheet in its template:</p>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`curl -fsSLo DESIGN.md https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dario-loi/polytope/v${version}/DESIGN.md
mkdir -p .impeccable
curl -fsSLo .impeccable/design.json https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dario-loi/polytope/v${version}/.impeccable/design.json`} />
  <p>With those files in place, Impeccable builds every new page inside Polytope and its design checker flags anything off the system, such as a font Polytope does not use. Then run <code>/impeccable init</code> in Claude Code so the site gets its own <code>PRODUCT.md</code>: who it is for, what it is for, and its real content.</p>

  <h2>Python</h2>
  <p>The figure and app themes are on PyPI as <code>polytope-theme</code>:</p>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`pip install polytope-theme
# with the libraries you use:
pip install "polytope-theme[matplotlib,plotly]"`} />

  <h2>No install at all</h2>
  <p>The docs site serves the built kit, so any static page can link it:</p>
  <Code lang="html" code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://dario-loi.github.io/polytope/kit/polytope.css">
<script type="module" src="https://dario-loi.github.io/polytope/kit/js/all.js"></script>`} />
  <Note kind="soft">Hosted files follow the latest release. Pin a version with npm when a page must never change.</Note>

  <h2>Working on the kit itself</h2>
  <Code lang="sh" code={`git clone https://github.com/dario-loi/polytope
cd polytope
npm install          # build dependencies
npm run build        # rebuilds dist/; commit the result
npm run docs:dev     # rebuilds the kit, starts this site
npm run check:contrast`} />
  <p>Edit tokens in <code>tokens/tokens.json</code> and styles in <code>css/src/</code>. Never edit <code>dist/</code> by hand; the build overwrites it. Commit it after each build, because installs read it straight from the repository.</p>
</Docs>
